# Copy to frontend/.env.local for local development.
#
# You usually do NOT need this file at all. The frontend and the API deploy as
# one project, so the UI calls the API on its own origin:
#   - in development, Vite proxies /api to http://localhost:5000 (vite.config.js)
#   - in production, the root vercel.json rewrites /api/* to backend/server.js
# Both cases use a relative /api path, so nothing has to be configured.
#
# The VITE_ prefix is required. Vite only exposes variables that start with it,
# so a variable named API_URL reads as undefined in the browser.
#
# Set this ONLY if the API genuinely lives on a different origin, in which case
# that origin also has to be listed in the backend's CLIENT_ORIGINS.
#
# Absolute base URL, no trailing slash:
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend.vercel.app
VITE_API_URL=
